cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Alpha Mining: An LLM-Agent Pipeline for Formulaic Alpha Discovery on WorldQuant BRAIN"
message: "If you use this repository or its research archive, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Li"
    given-names: "Zequn"
repository-code: "https://github.com/zl3311/alpha-mining"
abstract: >-
  An archived LLM-agent pipeline that discovered, backtested, and submitted formulaic
  trading alphas on the WorldQuant BRAIN platform, published together with the complete
  research log it produced: 63 mining sessions, 68 submitted-alpha records across 60
  mechanism families, 1,669 per-field factor profiles, and 28 documented dead ends.
  The system used no planner or reinforcement learning; iteration compounded through a
  file-based knowledge base that a language model read and appended to each session.
keywords:
  - quantitative-finance
  - alpha-mining
  - large-language-models
  - llm-agents
  - factor-investing
  - worldquant-brain
  - agent-skills
  - research-archive
